      "text": "We need to find the average number of rounds played by each golfer. To do this, we need to find the sum of the number of rounds played by all the golfers, and then divide by the total number of golfers.\n\nWe can count the number of golfers in each column using a picture. Counting the picture, we see that there are 15 golfers who played 1 round, 8 golfers who played 2 rounds, 5 golfers who played 3 rounds, 3 golfers who played 4 rounds, and 2 golfers who played 5 rounds. \n\nNext, we will add the number of golfers who played 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 rounds. We find this summary:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rc}$1$ & 15\\\\$2$ &8\\\\$3$ & 5\\\\$4$ &3\\\\$5$ & 2\\end{array}.$$\n\nThen, we will add all those numbers to find the total number of rounds played:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rc}$1$ & 15\\\\$2$ &8\\\\$3$ & 5\\\\$4$ &3\\\\$5$ & 2\\end{array}= 34.$$\n\nFinally, we can find the average number of rounds played by each golfer by dividing the total of rounds played by the total number of golfers in the chart:\n\n$$\\dfrac{34}{15}= 2.27.$$\n\nTherefore, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is $\\boxed{2}.$",
