      "text": "First, we need to find the total number of rounds played by all the golfers. Looking at the chart, we see that there are 5 golfers who played 1 round, 2 golfers who played 2 rounds, 2 golfers who played 3 rounds, 3 golfers who played 4 rounds, and 5 golfers who played 5 rounds. The total number of rounds played is:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n1(5) + 2(2) + 3(2) + 4(3) + 5(5) &= 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 \\\\\n&= 52\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nNext, we need to find the total number of golfers. Looking at the chart, we see that there are 5 golfers who played 1 round, 2 golfers who played 2 rounds, 2 golfers who played 3 rounds, 3 golfers who played 4 rounds, and 5 golfers who played 5 rounds. The total number of golfers is:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 &= 17\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nNow we can calculate the average number of rounds played by each golfer:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Average} &= \\frac{\\text{Total rounds}}{\\text{Total golfers}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{52}{17} \\\\\n&\\approx \\boxed{3}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe final answer is 3.",
