      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we first need to find the total number of rounds played by all the golfers. We can do this by adding up the number of rounds played by each golfer.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see that:\n\n- The 1st golfer played 5 rounds.\n- The 2nd golfer played 2 rounds.\n- The 3rd golfer played 2 rounds.\n- The 4th golfer played 3 rounds.\n- The 5th golfer played 5 rounds.\n\nAdding these together, we get a total of $5+2+2+3+5=17$ rounds played by all the golfers.\n\nNext, we need to find the total number of golfers. From the chart, we can see that there are 5 golfers.\n\nFinally, to find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we divide the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers:\n\n$$\\frac{17}{5}=3.4\\text{ rounds per golfer}.$$\n\nRounding this to the nearest whole number, we get $\\boxed{3}$.The answer is: 3",
